+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Visitors who only want a board for an afternoon are turned away, because rentals can only be priced and booked in whole days. Renting by the hour lets the school serve them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`: the cost of one hour of rental, a non-negative integer number of euro cents.
+- A period shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour (UTC) is an hourly rental, priced at the item's `hourlyPrice` for each hour. No long-rental discount applies.
+- An item without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be quoted or booked by the hour; the request throws.
+- Hourly bookings take part in the no-overlap rule like any other booking, so they block overlapping day rentals and vice versa.
+- Whole-day periods, their pricing and the 10% long-rental discount are unchanged.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rental-booking`: equipment registration takes an optional `hourlyPrice`; the period rules admit hourly periods shorter than a day; quote pricing gains the hourly rule.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/rental.ts` (equipment validation, pricing) and `src/period.ts` (period parsing), with tests in `src/*.test.ts`.
+- `README.md` rental section.
+- No new dependencies. Existing callers that pass no `hourlyPrice` and whole-day periods behave as before.
